**Daglir** (/'*dɑɣlir*/, *[[himfahric|Himfahric]]*: 𐑛𐑭𐑡𐑤𐑽, romanized: Dadjlear, *[[ukrashan|Ukrashan]]*: *𐒆𐒖𐒌𐒐𐒕𐒇*, [[hiureno|Hiureno]]: *ᚇᚐᚌᚂᚔᚏ* ) is one of the seven elemental deities. He is bound to the element of Water and he is the god of the seas. The waves of the oceans have spread the word of Daglir far and wide.

-----

# Religion
The Dadjan religion lacks a building as a house of worship, yet they commune in specific built town squares. These squares are round and have tiny canals of water flowing throughout.^[Sqaures are usually built near rivers, to provide the water source. But in other instances they''ve learned to create artificial water sources.] The Dadjan communes aren't filled with stories and epics, but they are filled with song and dance. The ideals of Daglir have ever been described in songs. Most of these temples have been built near the docks and sailors leaving port usually take part in this commune before leaving port, even if they belong to a different religion.

A traditional Dadjan commune is held at dawn, the *Passeri*[^passeri] opens the ceremony with a custom written song. He usually writes a custom song to address the recent events and to assure the followers. Later he follows this up with the traditional everyone knows from the *Songr Vithr*[^sr]. The dance through dawn into the night. The faith magic from this communion works to shine moonlight to cover the square, with the light getting evermore colorful into the night.

The Dadjan religion is very refracted due to the lack of central authority. The beauty in this is that the sailors on the sea are able to practice a similar religion to those in the deserts. These people are in completely different climates, yet are united in faith. The Landinward version allows for the summoning of water in the deeps of the desert, while the Seabound version allows for a protected passage on a ship.

One of the stories sung in the *Songr Vithr* is the story of Daglir's ascension. The story starts with veil between the depths of the oceans and the Underdark breaking. He, Daglir, was a normal human living on this plane and had risen up the rank to become a leading officer on the battlefield. After the veil broke and horrific creatures from the Underdark climbed ashore, he was in the first line of defense. After hours and hours of battle he was stricken down fatally. His last words to his son was, carry on, don't let them know. His son took his helmet and commanded the army to a glistering victory.^[Inspired by the *Death of Admiral Yi Sun-Sin*]

After he had died and his spirit had left his body, it was caught by the Preceding Deity of Water, she had given him the physical body of her Sea Serpent *Sidrim*. Eventually she would pass away as a deity and Daglir would succeed her as the Water Deity.
## Sects
- Dogma of **Speki**[^speki]
	The Dogma of Speki are the archivists following Daglir, usually living in the bigger of cities. They have kept seas of knowledge in their libraries.
- Dogma of **Mani**[^mani]
	The Dogma of Mani are moon focused part of Dadjan religion. They usually commune at midnight, instead of dusk, and their moonlight shines even brighter.
- Dogma of **Saer**[^saer]
	The Dogma of Saer are the seabound sailors. They only exist in port cities, as it is open to everyone going to sea.
- Dogma of **Vertrar**[^vertrar]
	The Dogma of Vertrar has learned the way of Water and learned to apply it to snow. The manage to curve snow away from their place of commuion.
## Structure
### Venerated Ancestors
*See also: [[list-of-dadjan-venerated-ancestors|List of Dadjan Venerated Ancestors]]*
The Dadjan religion employs a form of venerated ancestors. The choose to venerate certain ancestors, who did wonderful acts within the religion, during certain time periods. The new covenant of the *Songr Vithr*[^sr] describes these songs. These venerated ancestor are given the prefix *Dor'e*[^dore] as a title. %%Dore is a lord title in Kannada%%

### Priestly Order
%%Named After Songbirds%%
The *Passeri*[^passeri] is the religious leader during a ceremony. These are appointed locally and write their own songs. They usually aren't ranked under anyone, yet in larger cities with multiple communities the *Oscines*[^oscines] leads the *Passeri*. 

# Cultural

## Wailing Remembrance
Wailing Remembrance is the Holy Day of Daglir. On this followers of Daglir from far and wide make their way to a sea side temple. The take part in a prolonged communion following into a grand feast.

This Holy day has gathered many traditions that have been passed down over time. One such tradition is the wearing of blue clothing. It is said that during this day all who wear blue will be blessed with good luck. Another tradition is that any follower of Daglir may go to a nearby beach and dive into the icecold waves. Those who do so will gain the blessing of Daglir.

## Songr Vithr[^sr]
The *Songr Vithr* is a ancient artifact which was written by Daglir himself. It is a grand epic of different songs, which tell us about the great feats he performed, as well as the tragedies he faced. Form this songbook we learn the mythological story of Daglir's ascension. The Songr Vithr also includes the lore of the Sea Serpent *Sidrim* and how the two became one. This book has been passed down through generations, and is still used today to teach children about the history of Daglir.

Later on, when Ancestor veneration was introduced to the religion, the New Covenant was added to include the songs for the venerated ancestors songs. The New Covenant includes 28 songs in total, four for each month. %%Like the new testament%%

